    "A": "Research the low-memory streaming path. Refine the measured S-row ring-buffer approach (0.05453 s): read each matrix value once, maintain 64-bit vertical sums, and scan all horizontal windows. Test input and scan changes independently; retain the full-matrix implementation as a comparison. The measured tiled-transpose variant was slower (0.08441 s), so do not assume an extra transpose helps. Preserve correctness for negative values and every valid N,S.",
    "B": "Research the serial contiguous row-major path, focusing on input throughput and the vertical-update kernel. Compare a buffered integer parser with the current scanf path, and assess compiler-vectorized scalar loops before considering further hand-written SIMD: explicit NEON measured 0.05581 s versus 0.05573 s for the scalar candidate. Measure parser and kernel changes separately, keep intermediate sums 64-bit, and avoid transpose unless measurements justify it.",
