    "analysis": "The given serpentine traversal updates O(S) values per window move, giving roughly O(S(N-S+1)^2) work, while the measured rolling-sum candidates reduce the main work to O(N^2). Baseline mean time is 0.12576 s; the fastest candidate is 0.05420 s (about 2.32x faster). The leading candidates are close, and the transpose and explicit-NEON measurements provide evidence against assuming those changes help. The target is ARM64 with four CPU cores. Keep experiments general for all valid inputs, preserve 64-bit intermediate arithmetic and output correctness, and evaluate integrations as whole programs."
